      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Thanks @Ms2ger for taking this on. I think @domenic will have to review the module bits, which seems like the most substantive change as at least per https://github.com/tc39/proposal-shadowrealm/issues/225#issuecomment-592159225 that's the main difference. Is that still a largely accurate summary?\r\n\r\nIt seems confusing that JS will continue using \"current Realm\", but we can't. Don't we only have to make the distinction for APIs that can be used inside a shadow realm? And only then in a limited number of cases? I'd prefer a solution where we don't introduce \"current underlying Realm\" as synonym for JS's \"current Realm\". (Apologies if we've discussed this before. It's been so long that I've forgotten most context.)",
